(6761823, 1011459, 67152, '<td valign="top">First off, you have a very pretty cat and you did a nice job to capture the details of its face/ fur.<br/> <br/>Now for a critique - I gave your shot a 7 for good quality photography and meeting the challenge - but I took time with each entry to figure out how the image met the criteria and was generous in voting.  I think many of the voters in the challenge expected to see the cat upside down or photographed in such a way so it looked upside down.  Taking an photo of an upside down subject and inverting it so it was right side up was risky for this challenge.  Further, you were not aided in having ''physics'' on your side, such as a pony tail hanging, or drops dropping up and such.  In addition, most voters probably felt that minimal effort was needed to get the shot since it is a pet and obviously taken inside - that doesn''t suggest it wasn''t difficult to get - just that it was perceived to be easy to capture.  Finally, shots of household pets need to be remarkable to score well, or have significant humor factor and while this was solid, it was neither humorous or amazing from a lighting etc perspective.</td>', 'First off, you have a very pretty cat and you did a nice job to capture the details of its face/ fur. Now for a critique - I gave your shot a 7 for good quality photography and meeting the challenge - but I took time with each entry to figure out how the image met the criteria and was generous in voting.  I think many of the voters in the challenge expected to see the cat upside down or photographed in such a way so it looked upside down.  Taking an photo of an upside down subject and inverting it so it was right side up was risky for this challenge.  Further, you were not aided in having ''physics'' on your side, such as a pony tail hanging, or drops dropping up and such.  In addition, most voters probably felt that minimal effort was needed to get the shot since it is a pet and obviously taken inside - that doesn''t suggest it wasn''t difficult to get - just that it was perceived to be easy to capture.  Finally, shots of household pets need to be remarkable to score well, or have significant humor factor and while this was solid, it was neither humorous or amazing from a lighting etc perspective.', '2012-05-07 08:17:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(6761827, 1011465, 120171, '<td valign="top">Congrats Lydia on a wonderful idea and a deserved win. Love the description if how the shoot came to be.</td>', 'Congrats Lydia on a wonderful idea and a deserved win. Love the description if how the shoot came to be.', '2012-05-07 08:20:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(6761828, 1012500, 67152, '<td valign="top">Jon - a funny facial expression, a fun shot for FB, but the background (the floor and sofa cutting a line across the top of the head) make this feel very ''snapshot'' like.  I gave it a 5 because it met challenge but it was otherwise unremarkable.</td>', 'Jon - a funny facial expression, a fun shot for FB, but the background (the floor and sofa cutting a line across the top of the head) make this feel very ''snapshot'' like.  I gave it a 5 because it met challenge but it was otherwise unremarkable.', '2012-05-07 08:20:33.000000', NULL, 0),
